From 92debdde7453c4d49fe9939f3e1f25b8e204c90f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrija Panic <andrija.panic@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:58:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] convert_windows: do not abort the pnputil firstboot script on
 one failing driver

The "pnputil install drivers" firstboot script exited 249 (retry on
next boot) as soon as one .inf failed to install, and the firstboot
wrapper retries 249 without limit.  A driver that fails
deterministically therefore rebooted the guest forever and blocked
every later firstboot script (QEMU guest agent, network configuration).
Seen on Windows Server 2025 with smbus.inf from virtio-win 0.1.285:
"A certificate chain processed, but terminated in a root certificate
which is not trusted by the trust provider."
https://github.com/libguestfs/virt-v2v/issues/178

Install every driver, remember the ones that failed, report them at the
end and exit 0.  By the time this script runs the guest has already
booted from its virtio disk, so no driver installed here can be a
prerequisite for booting; a missing optional device driver is a
degraded guest, an endless reboot loop is an unusable one.  The
pending-reboot check keeps its 249.

Signed-off-by: Andrija Panic <andrija.panic@gmail.com>

Backport to virt-v2v 2.7.1 (rhel-9.8) of upstream commit
fe53f740c189af69137b008694bf2b0a239ef273, pull request
https://github.com/libguestfs/virt-v2v/pull/202, released in
virt-v2v 2.13.8.  Rewritten by hand: rhel-9.8 carries the same script
(Red Hat's backports of 594b05d6, 523aff28 and 07192e2b) in the older
"...\n\" string form, so the upstream change does not apply as is.
The script logic is the same as upstream's.

One line added downstream: when a reboot is pending, the script also
says "No drivers were installed by pnputil on this attempt.", so that
the first-boot log states plainly that pnputil installed nothing if the
first-boot service gives up after 3 attempts (patch 9007).
---
 convert/convert_windows.ml | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/convert/convert_windows.ml b/convert/convert_windows.ml
index b80128a7..6c8a6688 100644
--- a/convert/convert_windows.ml
+++ b/convert/convert_windows.ml
@@ -421,21 +421,29 @@ let convert (g : G.guestfs) source inspect i_firmware
                      \n\
                      if \"%REBOOT_PENDING%\"==\"1\" (\n\
                      echo A reboot is pending.\n\
+                     echo No drivers were installed by pnputil on this attempt.\n\
                      exit /b 249\n\
                      ) else (\n\
                      echo No pending reboot detected.\n\
                      )\n\
                      \n\
+                     set FAILED=\n\
                      for %%f in (\"%inf_dir%*.inf\") do (\n\
                      echo Installing: %%~nxf.\n\
                      %systemroot%\\Sysnative\\PnPutil -i -a \"%%f\"\n\
                      if !errorlevel! neq 0 if !errorlevel! neq 259 (\n\
-                     echo Failed to install %%~nxf.\n\
-                     exit /b 249\n\
+                     echo Failed to install %%~nxf ^(pnputil exit code !errorlevel!^).\n\
+                     set FAILED=!FAILED! %%~nxf\n\
                      ) else (\n\
                      echo Successfully installed %%~nxf.\n\
                      )\n\
                      )\n\
+                     if defined FAILED (\n\
+                     echo The following drivers could not be installed:!FAILED!\n\
+                     echo The guest has already booted from its virtio disk, so a driver that\n\
+                     echo fails deterministically must not block the remaining firstboot scripts.\n\
+                     exit /b 0\n\
+                     )\n\
                      echo All drivers installed successfully.\n\
                      exit /b 0\n\
                      )" in
-- 
